# Normalize to LF in the repository. Windows working copies still get CRLF via
# core.autocrlf, but what is *stored* no longer depends on each contributor's git config.
#
# This is not cosmetic. deploy/install.sh is tarred from a Linux runner straight onto the
# target host: a single CRLF in the shebang turns it into `/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and the host
# reports "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" - naming a file that plainly exists.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files where a CR is fatal rather than untidy.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# Ground truth is UTF-8 with meaningful full-width punctuation; never touch it.
*.jpwabc    text eol=lf working-tree-encoding=UTF-8
